TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` attributes with a scope enum, plus class hooks via `IClassConstructor` / `IAsyncInitializer` / `IAsyncDisposable`. Here's a sketch for each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // runs after each [Test]
    }

    [Test]
    public void SomeTest() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests : IAsyncInitializer, IAsyncDisposable
{
    private ServiceFixture _fixture;

    public async Task InitializeAsync()
    {
        // once before the first test in this class
        _fixture = await ServiceFixture.StartAsync();
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        // once after the last test in this class
        await _fixture.DisposeAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public void TestOne() { /* ... */ }
}

// Or use the hook attribute approach:
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void SetUp() { /* once before first test */ }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void TearDown() { /* once after last test */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Per Assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        // runs once before any test in the assembly
        WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it by attribute.

## 4. Once Per Entire Test Session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class SessionLifecycle
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations()
    {
        // very first thing in the run
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task DestroyDatabase()
    {
        // very last thing in the run
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

**Summary table:**

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be |
|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` |

The enum values come from `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;`. All hooks support `async Task` or `async ValueTask` return types. Class-level and above must be `static`; test-level hooks are instance methods.
